# Used by `go run ./cmd/api` directly against `docker compose up postgres`.
# When running the full stack (`docker compose up`), only JWT_SECRET, the
# SMTP_* vars below, and optionally SITE_ADDRESS matter - PORT/DATABASE_URL
# are set for the containerized api service in docker-compose.yml.
PORT=8080
DATABASE_URL=postgres://scheduler:scheduler@localhost:5432/scheduler?sslmode=disable

# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-random-32+-char-secret

# Domain Caddy serves HTTPS on. Leave unset for local dev (defaults to
# "localhost" + a self-signed cert). Set to a real domain in production and
# Caddy fetches a real Let's Encrypt cert automatically.
SITE_ADDRESS=localhost

# Outgoing mail for the verify-email / forgot-password OTP codes
# (internal/mailer) - a real authenticated SMTP relay, required (the api
# process refuses to start without these). net/smtp negotiates STARTTLS on
# its own, so any provider's plain SMTP endpoint works here, no extra
# config. Example values below are for Gmail:
#
#   1. Turn on 2-Step Verification on the Google account.
#   2. Google Account -> Security -> 2-Step Verification -> App passwords
#      -> create one for "Mail". That 16-character password is
#      SMTP_PASSWORD below - not the account's real password.
#   3. SMTP_FROM must match SMTP_USER (or a verified alias) or Gmail
#      rejects the send.
#
# Any other provider's SMTP credentials (SES, Brevo, Resend, etc) work the
# same way - just swap the host/port/user/password.
SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_FROM=youraddress@gmail.com
SMTP_USER=youraddress@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-gmail-app-password
